# Every version of every built-in file the binary has carried, one
# `sha256sum` line each (docs/builtin-updates.md).
#
# A seeded copy whose hash is listed here for its path was written by this
# program and edited by nobody, so a newer release may replace it; any other
# copy is the user's and is never written over.
#
# NEVER REMOVE A LINE. When a file under prompts/skills or prompts/agents
# changes, append its new version (a failing test names the exact command):
#
#   sha256sum prompts/skills/<name>/<file> >> prompts/shipped.sha256
#
# Removing a line turns every install that still has that version into "an
# edit": kept for good and never updated again. `scripts/shipped_history.sh
# --check` (CI) holds the list to every version this repository's history
# ever carried.
#
# A path's FIRST line is the version every release up to v0.19.0 shipped —
# the base assumed for an edited copy that has no record. Keep it first.

